1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,008
What's today's video about? It's Travel Japanese Conversation!

2
00:00:10,008 --> 00:00:11,508
Scene 1: Buying a Ticket / How to Buy a Train Ticket

3
00:00:11,508 --> 00:00:13,604
Excuse me.

4
00:00:13,627 --> 00:00:16,478
Yes, how can I help you?

5
00:00:16,501 --> 00:00:19,788
I'd like to go to Tokyo Station.

6
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:22,179
Tokyo Station, right?

7
00:00:22,202 --> 00:00:26,402
Yes, where can I buy a ticket?

8
00:00:26,425 --> 00:00:29,859
You can buy it at the ticket vending machine over there.

9
00:00:29,882 --> 00:00:32,782
That blue machine?

10
00:00:32,805 --> 00:00:35,742
Yes, that's the one.

11
00:00:35,766 --> 00:00:39,299
I don’t know how to use the ticket machine.

12
00:00:39,322 --> 00:00:41,892
Let me go with you.

13
00:00:41,915 --> 00:00:43,984
Thank you so much.

14
00:00:44,008 --> 00:00:46,142
That really helps.

15
00:00:46,165 --> 00:00:49,184
Please press English on the screen.

16
00:00:49,207 --> 00:00:52,375
Okay, I pressed it.

17
00:00:52,398 --> 00:00:55,765
Next, press Tokyo Station.

18
00:00:55,788 --> 00:00:58,232
Tokyo Station, right?

19
00:00:58,255 --> 00:01:00,227
Found it.

20
00:01:00,251 --> 00:01:02,268
Adult?

21
00:01:02,292 --> 00:01:03,925
Child?

22
00:01:03,948 --> 00:01:06,881
Two adults.

23
00:01:06,904 --> 00:01:10,271
Then, select two people.

24
00:01:10,294 --> 00:01:12,460
This one, right?

25
00:01:12,483 --> 00:01:14,617
How much is it?

26
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:17,488
It's 1,500 yen.

27
00:01:17,511 --> 00:01:20,590
Where do I insert the money?

28
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:23,747
Please insert the money here.

29
00:01:23,770 --> 00:01:27,005
Can I use a credit card?

30
00:01:27,029 --> 00:01:30,285
Yes, you can.

31
00:01:30,308 --> 00:01:32,482
I’ll insert the card.

32
00:01:32,506 --> 00:01:35,539
Please enter your PIN.

33
00:01:35,562 --> 00:01:38,229
Okay, done.

34
00:01:38,252 --> 00:01:40,618
The ticket will come out now.

35
00:01:40,641 --> 00:01:43,975
I’ve received two tickets.

36
00:01:43,998 --> 00:01:46,731
Don’t forget them.

37
00:01:46,754 --> 00:01:50,354
Which platform does the train leave from?

38
00:01:50,377 --> 00:01:53,274
It leaves from Platform 3.

39
00:01:53,297 --> 00:01:55,710
Platform 3, right?

40
00:01:55,734 --> 00:01:57,872
Is it over there?

41
00:01:57,896 --> 00:02:02,062
No, it's downstairs to the left.

42
00:02:02,085 --> 00:02:05,860
Downstairs to the left, got it.

43
00:02:05,884 --> 00:02:09,264
The train arrives in 10 minutes.

44
00:02:09,287 --> 00:02:11,654
Is it an express train?

45
00:02:11,676 --> 00:02:14,947
Yes, it's an express train.

46
00:02:14,971 --> 00:02:17,771
Do I need to transfer?

47
00:02:17,794 --> 00:02:21,728
No, there’s no transfer.

48
00:02:21,751 --> 00:02:23,917
It goes straight there.

49
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,274
That’s great!

50
00:02:26,297 --> 00:02:29,464
Thank you so much for your kindness.

51
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:34,220
You're welcome. Please take care and have a safe trip!

52
00:02:34,243 --> 00:02:43,252
You can download today's video script from the description and top comment. Please leave a comment before downloading!

53
00:02:43,252 --> 00:02:44,752
Scene 2: Hotel Check-In – A Smooth Process

54
00:02:44,752 --> 00:02:46,919
Welcome!

55
00:02:46,942 --> 00:02:48,709
Hello.

56
00:02:48,732 --> 00:02:50,498
Hello.

57
00:02:50,521 --> 00:02:53,900
I’d like to check in, please.

58
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:58,393
May I have your name, please?

59
00:02:58,417 --> 00:03:00,783
Smith.

60
00:03:00,806 --> 00:03:03,473
Mr. Smith, correct?

61
00:03:03,496 --> 00:03:07,029
Let me confirm your reservation.

62
00:03:07,052 --> 00:03:11,068
Yes, please.

63
00:03:11,091 --> 00:03:15,025
You’re staying for two nights starting today, is that right?

64
00:03:15,048 --> 00:03:18,507
Yes, two nights.

65
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:23,264
Your room is a non-smoking double.

66
00:03:23,287 --> 00:03:26,384
That’s correct.

67
00:03:26,408 --> 00:03:30,585
Please fill in your name and address here.

68
00:03:30,608 --> 00:03:33,808
Could I borrow a pen?

69
00:03:33,831 --> 00:03:37,508
Of course, here you go.

70
00:03:37,532 --> 00:03:39,699
All done.

71
00:03:39,722 --> 00:03:42,620
Do you need my passport?

72
00:03:42,643 --> 00:03:46,477
Yes, may I see your passport?

73
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:49,633
Here you are.

74
00:03:49,656 --> 00:03:51,623
Thank you so much.

75
00:03:51,646 --> 00:03:54,379
I’ll make a copy.

76
00:03:54,402 --> 00:03:57,899
Okay, got it.

77
00:03:57,923 --> 00:03:59,730
Thank you for waiting.

78
00:03:59,754 --> 00:04:02,021
Here’s your room key.

79
00:04:02,044 --> 00:04:04,777
What floor is my room on?

80
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:08,833
It’s room 502 on the 5th floor.

81
00:04:08,856 --> 00:04:11,754
Where are the elevators?

82
00:04:11,778 --> 00:04:15,179
They’re right over there on the right.

83
00:04:15,202 --> 00:04:16,936
Thank you so much.

84
00:04:16,959 --> 00:04:19,759
What time does breakfast start?

85
00:04:19,782 --> 00:04:24,715
Breakfast is from 7:00 AM to 10:00 AM.

86
00:04:24,738 --> 00:04:27,989
Where is the breakfast served?

87
00:04:28,012 --> 00:04:31,990
In the restaurant on the first floor.

88
00:04:32,014 --> 00:04:34,814
What’s the Wi-Fi password?

89
00:04:34,837 --> 00:04:38,495
It’s written on the back of your keycard.

90
00:04:38,518 --> 00:04:41,484
Oh, you’re right!

91
00:04:41,507 --> 00:04:43,923
It’s there.

92
00:04:43,947 --> 00:04:47,581
You’re also welcome to use our large public bath.

93
00:04:47,604 --> 00:04:50,937
What floor is the public bath on?

94
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,360
It’s on the second floor.

95
00:04:53,383 --> 00:04:56,116
What are the hours for the public bath?

96
00:04:56,139 --> 00:05:00,388
From 3:00 PM to midnight.

97
00:05:00,412 --> 00:05:03,751
Should I bring towels from my room?

98
00:05:03,774 --> 00:05:08,174
Yes, please bring the towels from your room.

99
00:05:08,197 --> 00:05:10,264
Understood.

100
00:05:10,287 --> 00:05:14,054
Could someone take my luggage to my room?

101
00:05:14,077 --> 00:05:18,143
Yes, our staff will bring it up shortly.

102
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:19,742
Thank you so much.

103
00:05:19,766 --> 00:05:21,533
Thank you.

104
00:05:21,555 --> 00:05:25,889
Enjoy your stay!

105
00:05:25,912 --> 00:05:33,017
Find the link to review today’s video in the description and top comment! *Note: The site may be removed without notice.

106
00:05:33,017 --> 00:05:34,517
Scene 3: Restaurant Reservation and Seating – A Warm Welcome Awaits

107
00:05:34,517 --> 00:05:36,410
Welcome!

108
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:38,730
For how many people?

109
00:05:38,754 --> 00:05:42,120
Two, please.

110
00:05:42,143 --> 00:05:46,943
Would you prefer a non-smoking or smoking section?

111
00:05:46,966 --> 00:05:50,416
Non-smoking, please.

112
00:05:50,439 --> 00:05:52,844
Right this way.

113
00:05:52,868 --> 00:05:56,302
Please take a seat wherever you'd like.

114
00:05:56,325 --> 00:05:59,491
Would a table by the window work for you?

115
00:05:59,514 --> 00:06:02,281
Here you are.

116
00:06:02,304 --> 00:06:03,987
Thank you!

117
00:06:04,011 --> 00:06:06,690
Could we get some water, please?

118
00:06:06,714 --> 00:06:11,047
Of course! I’ll bring you some cold water right away.

119
00:06:11,070 --> 00:06:13,637
Could we see the menu as well?

120
00:06:13,660 --> 00:06:16,793
Here’s the menu for you.

121
00:06:16,816 --> 00:06:20,216
We also have an English menu available.

122
00:06:20,239 --> 00:06:23,328
The English menu, please.

123
00:06:23,351 --> 00:06:26,821
Certainly! Just a moment, please.

124
00:06:26,845 --> 00:06:30,678
What’s the most popular dish here?

125
00:06:30,701 --> 00:06:34,435
Our pork cutlet set meal is the most popular.

126
00:06:34,458 --> 00:06:37,024
That sounds delicious!

127
00:06:37,047 --> 00:06:39,414
What does it taste like?

128
00:06:39,437 --> 00:06:44,404
The meat is tender, and the sauce is sweet.

129
00:06:44,427 --> 00:06:48,476
Then I’ll have the pork cutlet set meal.

130
00:06:48,499 --> 00:06:52,539
Got it—one pork cutlet set meal.

131
00:06:52,563 --> 00:06:56,329
One of my friends can’t eat pork.

132
00:06:56,352 --> 00:06:59,786
We also have fish dishes available.

133
00:06:59,809 --> 00:07:03,895
Do you have a sashimi set meal?

134
00:07:03,918 --> 00:07:09,285
Yes, we have today’s recommended sashimi set meal.

135
00:07:09,308 --> 00:07:13,376
Then I’ll have the sashimi set meal as well.

136
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:16,199
Understood.

137
00:07:16,222 --> 00:07:19,989
Can we choose the portion size for the rice?

138
00:07:20,012 --> 00:07:24,978
You can choose from large, regular, or small portions.

139
00:07:25,001 --> 00:07:28,234
Both as regular size, please.

140
00:07:28,257 --> 00:07:32,343
Would you like anything to drink?

141
00:07:32,367 --> 00:07:35,863
Two draft beers, please.

142
00:07:35,887 --> 00:07:39,583
Should we bring the drinks first?

143
00:07:39,607 --> 00:07:43,007
Yes, please bring them first.

144
00:07:43,030 --> 00:07:45,263
Certainly.

145
00:07:45,286 --> 00:07:47,853
Let me confirm your order.

146
00:07:47,876 --> 00:07:50,009
Yes, please.

147
00:07:50,032 --> 00:07:58,638
One pork cutlet set meal, one sashimi set meal, and two draft beers—is that correct?

148
00:07:58,661 --> 00:08:01,428
Is wasabi okay with your sashimi?

149
00:08:01,451 --> 00:08:05,184
Please hold the wasabi for the sashimi.

150
00:08:05,207 --> 00:08:07,441
Understood.

151
00:08:07,464 --> 00:08:08,964
Scene 4: The Art of Customer Service – Making Every Guest Feel Valued

152
00:08:08,964 --> 00:08:10,939
Welcome!

153
00:08:10,962 --> 00:08:13,440
Are you looking for something in particular?

154
00:08:13,464 --> 00:08:17,064
Can I take a look at this T-shirt?

155
00:08:17,087 --> 00:08:18,545
Of course!

156
00:08:18,568 --> 00:08:22,101
Please feel free to pick it up and have a closer look.

157
00:08:22,124 --> 00:08:25,411
Do you have this in a medium size?

158
00:08:25,435 --> 00:08:28,603
Let me check for you.

159
00:08:28,626 --> 00:08:30,901
Just a moment, please.

160
00:08:30,925 --> 00:08:32,458
Of course!

161
00:08:32,481 --> 00:08:34,514
Thank you.

162
00:08:34,537 --> 00:08:36,704
Thank you for waiting.

163
00:08:36,727 --> 00:08:39,329
Here's the medium size.

164
00:08:39,353 --> 00:08:41,047
Thank you so much.

165
00:08:41,070 --> 00:08:43,527
Can I try this on?

166
00:08:43,551 --> 00:08:45,204
Of course!

167
00:08:45,228 --> 00:08:48,161
Of course, you may try it on.

168
00:08:48,184 --> 00:08:50,464
Where are the fitting rooms?

169
00:08:50,487 --> 00:08:53,421
They're right over there at the back.

170
00:08:53,444 --> 00:08:55,810
I'll try it on.

171
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,700
How does it feel?

172
00:08:57,723 --> 00:09:00,060
It fits perfectly!

173
00:09:00,083 --> 00:09:02,483
I'll take this one.

174
00:09:02,506 --> 00:09:04,440
Thank you so much.

175
00:09:04,463 --> 00:09:07,269
Would you like to see other colors?

176
00:09:07,292 --> 00:09:10,259
Do you have this in black?

177
00:09:10,282 --> 00:09:11,915
Of course!

178
00:09:11,938 --> 00:09:15,017
We have black, white, and blue.

179
00:09:15,041 --> 00:09:18,508
Can I see the black in medium as well?

180
00:09:18,530 --> 00:09:20,387
Of course!

181
00:09:20,411 --> 00:09:23,450
Here's the black in medium.

182
00:09:23,474 --> 00:09:26,089
This looks great too!

183
00:09:26,112 --> 00:09:28,408
I'll take both.

184
00:09:28,432 --> 00:09:30,074
Thank you so much.

185
00:09:30,097 --> 00:09:33,513
Would you like some local snacks as souvenirs?

186
00:09:33,537 --> 00:09:36,770
Do you have any famous local snacks?

187
00:09:36,793 --> 00:09:40,651
Our matcha cookies are very popular.

188
00:09:40,675 --> 00:09:43,275
I'll take three boxes of those.

189
00:09:43,298 --> 00:09:45,708
Certainly.

190
00:09:45,731 --> 00:09:48,064
Please proceed to the checkout.

191
00:09:48,087 --> 00:09:50,487
Is tax-free available?

192
00:09:50,510 --> 00:09:55,544
Since your purchase exceeds 5,000 yen, you qualify for tax-free.

193
00:09:55,567 --> 00:09:57,733
I have my passport.

194
00:09:57,756 --> 00:10:00,971
May I see your passport, please?

195
00:10:00,995 --> 00:10:02,246
Of course!

196
00:10:02,270 --> 00:10:04,080
Here you go.

197
00:10:04,103 --> 00:10:07,037
Your total comes to 6,000 yen.

198
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:10,074
Can I pay with a credit card?

199
00:10:10,097 --> 00:10:11,792
Of course!

200
00:10:11,815 --> 00:10:14,483
You can also use contactless payment.

201
00:10:14,507 --> 00:10:16,674
I'll pay with my card.

202
00:10:16,697 --> 00:10:19,430
Please tap your card here.

203
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:21,086
Of course!

204
00:10:21,109 --> 00:10:22,843
Tapped.

205
00:10:22,866 --> 00:10:24,485
Thank you so much.

206
00:10:24,508 --> 00:10:27,241
Here's your receipt and passport.

207
00:10:27,265 --> 00:10:30,635
Could you put them in a bag for me?

208
00:10:30,659 --> 00:10:31,793
Of course!

209
00:10:31,817 --> 00:10:35,219
I'll put them in a large bag for you.

210
00:10:35,242 --> 00:10:36,909
Thank you so much.

211
00:10:36,932 --> 00:10:38,780
That helps a lot, thanks!

212
00:10:38,803 --> 00:10:41,737
Have a wonderful trip!

213
00:10:41,760 --> 00:10:43,260
Scene 5: Shopping Conversation Basics

214
00:10:43,260 --> 00:10:45,426
Welcome!

215
00:10:45,449 --> 00:10:46,909
Excuse me.

216
00:10:46,932 --> 00:10:49,899
Where can I find hot tea?

217
00:10:49,922 --> 00:10:54,255
It's at the hot beverage corner near the entrance.

218
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:55,912
Thank you so much.

219
00:10:55,935 --> 00:10:57,940
I'll take a look.

220
00:10:57,964 --> 00:11:01,039
Are you looking for something in particular?

221
00:11:01,062 --> 00:11:03,679
Do you sell umbrellas?

222
00:11:03,702 --> 00:11:07,375
Yes, they're next to the shelf over there.

223
00:11:07,399 --> 00:11:12,068
I'll take a plastic umbrella and a bottle of tea.

224
00:11:12,091 --> 00:11:14,625
Would you like a bento as well?

225
00:11:14,648 --> 00:11:16,663
They're delicious!

226
00:11:16,686 --> 00:11:19,965
I'll take this fried chicken bento as well.

227
00:11:19,989 --> 00:11:22,522
Certainly.

228
00:11:22,545 --> 00:11:24,823
We'll take care of it at the register.

229
00:11:24,847 --> 00:11:27,126
Is this the checkout?

230
00:11:27,150 --> 00:11:29,883
Yes, right this way, please.

231
00:11:29,906 --> 00:11:33,073
Could you warm up my bento, please?

232
00:11:33,096 --> 00:11:35,829
Sure, I'll warm it up for you.

233
00:11:35,852 --> 00:11:38,219
Just a moment, please.

234
00:11:38,242 --> 00:11:40,619
How long will it take?

235
00:11:40,642 --> 00:11:43,442
It’ll be ready in about a minute.

236
00:11:43,465 --> 00:11:46,444
Could I get some chopsticks or a spoon?

237
00:11:46,467 --> 00:11:49,634
How many pairs of chopsticks would you like?

238
00:11:49,657 --> 00:11:51,890
One pair is fine.

239
00:11:51,913 --> 00:11:54,522
Would you like a spoon as well?

240
00:11:54,546 --> 00:11:56,844
No spoon, thanks.

241
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:59,758
Would you like a straw?

242
00:11:59,782 --> 00:12:03,248
It’s tea, so I don’t need a straw.

243
00:12:03,271 --> 00:12:05,238
Certainly.

244
00:12:05,261 --> 00:12:07,878
Will you be using a bag?

245
00:12:07,901 --> 00:12:10,399
Is the bag charged?

246
00:12:10,423 --> 00:12:13,956
Yes, it’s 3 yen per bag.

247
00:12:13,979 --> 00:12:17,226
Then I’ll take one bag, please.

248
00:12:17,249 --> 00:12:20,537
Alright, that’ll be an extra 3 yen.

249
00:12:20,561 --> 00:12:22,794
How much is the total?

250
00:12:22,817 --> 00:12:26,417
Your total comes to 850 yen.

251
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:28,812
I’ll pay in cash.

252
00:12:28,835 --> 00:12:30,872
I’ll give you 1,000 yen.

253
00:12:30,896 --> 00:12:33,429
Out of 1,000 yen, thank you.

254
00:12:33,452 --> 00:12:36,585
Here’s your change, 150 yen.

255
00:12:36,608 --> 00:12:38,855
Could I get the receipt as well?

256
00:12:38,879 --> 00:12:42,516
Of course, here’s your receipt.

257
00:12:42,539 --> 00:12:45,230
Is your bento warmed up?

258
00:12:45,254 --> 00:12:48,021
Yes, it’s ready.

259
00:12:48,044 --> 00:12:50,924
Careful, it’s hot!

260
00:12:50,948 --> 00:12:52,403
Thank you so much.

261
00:12:52,426 --> 00:12:55,559
I’ve put it in a takeout bag for you.

262
00:12:55,582 --> 00:12:58,820
Thanks for your great service!

263
00:12:58,844 --> 00:13:01,936
We look forward to your next visit!

264
00:13:01,959 --> 00:13:03,459
Scene 6: A Conversation About Taking Photos

265
00:13:03,459 --> 00:13:05,345
Excuse me.

266
00:13:05,368 --> 00:13:07,501
Excuse me, do you have a moment?

267
00:13:07,524 --> 00:13:10,592
Yes, how can I help?

268
00:13:10,615 --> 00:13:13,509
Could you take a photo of me, please?

269
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:15,266
Sure, I’d be happy to!

270
00:13:15,289 --> 00:13:17,959
Let’s take the photo.

271
00:13:17,982 --> 00:13:20,783
Please use this phone.

272
00:13:20,807 --> 00:13:22,645
Understood.

273
00:13:22,668 --> 00:13:25,202
Should I take it in landscape mode?

274
00:13:25,225 --> 00:13:28,004
Please take it in portrait mode.

275
00:13:28,027 --> 00:13:31,102
I’ll include the castle in the background.

276
00:13:31,125 --> 00:13:32,335
Of course!

277
00:13:32,358 --> 00:13:35,792
Make sure the castle is clearly visible.

278
00:13:35,816 --> 00:13:38,073
Are you ready?

279
00:13:38,096 --> 00:13:40,096
Here we go!

280
00:13:40,119 --> 00:13:42,086
Yes, please.

281
00:13:42,109 --> 00:13:46,482
Say cheese! *Click.*

282
00:13:46,505 --> 00:13:49,505
Could you take one more, please?

283
00:13:49,528 --> 00:13:51,366
Sure, I’d be happy to!

284
00:13:51,389 --> 00:13:54,081
Shall we try a different pose this time?

285
00:13:54,104 --> 00:13:55,504
Of course!

286
00:13:55,527 --> 00:13:58,494
Please take a smiling shot here.

287
00:13:58,517 --> 00:14:01,198
Alright, here we go!

288
00:14:01,221 --> 00:14:05,289
Three, two, one.

289
00:14:05,312 --> 00:14:07,112
Thank you so much.

290
00:14:07,135 --> 00:14:09,902
Let me check.

291
00:14:09,925 --> 00:14:11,596
Here you go.

292
00:14:11,620 --> 00:14:13,869
It looks great!

293
00:14:13,892 --> 00:14:15,692
Wow, it really does!

294
00:14:15,715 --> 00:14:18,182
You took that so well!

295
00:14:18,205 --> 00:14:20,459
That’s great!

296
00:14:20,482 --> 00:14:22,015
Are you sightseeing?

297
00:14:22,038 --> 00:14:25,440
Yes, I’m from the U.S.

298
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:27,097
I see.

299
00:14:27,121 --> 00:14:29,954
Are you enjoying Japan?

300
00:14:29,977 --> 00:14:33,177
Yes, I’m having a great time!

301
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:35,400
That’s wonderful to hear!

302
00:14:35,423 --> 00:14:39,423
Um, is there a restroom nearby?

303
00:14:39,446 --> 00:14:41,179
You mean the bathroom?

304
00:14:41,202 --> 00:14:44,499
It’s behind that big tree over there.

305
00:14:44,522 --> 00:14:47,322
Is it the building with the red roof?

306
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:51,122
No, it’s the one with the blue roof.

307
00:14:51,146 --> 00:14:53,154
The blue roof, got it.

308
00:14:53,178 --> 00:14:54,911
I see, thank you.

309
00:14:54,934 --> 00:14:58,334
There’s also an accessible restroom available.

310
00:14:58,357 --> 00:14:59,890
That really helps.

311
00:14:59,913 --> 00:15:02,786
Where are the coin lockers?

312
00:15:02,810 --> 00:15:06,496
The coin lockers are at the station entrance.

313
00:15:06,519 --> 00:15:09,495
How long does it take to walk there?

314
00:15:09,519 --> 00:15:12,138
About five minutes.

315
00:15:12,162 --> 00:15:13,930
That’s close!

316
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:15,820
That’s great!

317
00:15:15,843 --> 00:15:18,877
The weather’s perfect today, isn’t it?

318
00:15:18,900 --> 00:15:22,545
Yes, it’s a great day for a walk!

319
00:15:22,568 --> 00:15:26,181
Make sure to take lots of great photos!

320
00:15:26,204 --> 00:15:28,171
Yes, thank you!

321
00:15:28,194 --> 00:15:31,240
Have a wonderful day!

322
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:34,430
You too, have a great day!

323
00:15:34,453 --> 00:15:35,953
Scene 7: Route Guidance and Time Confirmation

324
00:15:35,953 --> 00:15:38,887
Thank you for riding with us.

325
00:15:38,910 --> 00:15:41,843
Where would you like to go?

326
00:15:41,866 --> 00:15:44,902
Tokyo Tower, please.

327
00:15:44,926 --> 00:15:47,292
Tokyo Tower, got it.

328
00:15:47,315 --> 00:15:49,253
Certainly.

329
00:15:49,277 --> 00:15:52,648
How long will it take?

330
00:15:52,672 --> 00:15:56,159
About 20 minutes if traffic isn’t bad.

331
00:15:56,182 --> 00:15:59,195
Is the road busy right now?

332
00:15:59,219 --> 00:16:03,252
There’s some construction, so it’s a bit busy.

333
00:16:03,275 --> 00:16:06,642
So, it might take around 30 minutes?

334
00:16:06,665 --> 00:16:08,603
That’s right.

335
00:16:08,626 --> 00:16:11,593
Please allow about 30 minutes.

336
00:16:11,616 --> 00:16:13,549
Understood.

337
00:16:13,572 --> 00:16:16,908
No rush, that’s fine.

338
00:16:16,932 --> 00:16:19,747
Would you like me to put your luggage in the trunk?

339
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:21,104
Of course!

340
00:16:21,127 --> 00:16:24,405
Yes, one suitcase, please.

341
00:16:24,429 --> 00:16:26,919
I’ll take care of it for you.

342
00:16:26,942 --> 00:16:29,775
It’s heavy, so please be careful.

343
00:16:29,798 --> 00:16:31,365
Thank you so much.

344
00:16:31,388 --> 00:16:33,721
We’re departing now.

345
00:16:33,744 --> 00:16:36,544
Please fasten your seatbelt.

346
00:16:36,567 --> 00:16:38,044
Of course!

347
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:39,701
All set.

348
00:16:39,723 --> 00:16:43,193
Shall we take the highway?

349
00:16:43,217 --> 00:16:45,854
Is it faster if we take the highway?

350
00:16:45,877 --> 00:16:47,311
Of course!

351
00:16:47,333 --> 00:16:50,421
It’ll save us about 10 minutes.

352
00:16:50,445 --> 00:16:53,978
Then let’s take the highway.

353
00:16:54,001 --> 00:16:56,239
Certainly.

354
00:16:56,262 --> 00:16:59,338
There’s an extra toll fee, though.

355
00:16:59,361 --> 00:17:01,161
Got it.

356
00:17:01,184 --> 00:17:03,436
No problem.

357
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:06,426
How’s the temperature? Too cold or too warm?

358
00:17:06,449 --> 00:17:10,183
It’s a bit chilly—could you turn it down?

359
00:17:10,207 --> 00:17:12,307
I’ll lower it for you.

360
00:17:12,330 --> 00:17:14,797
How’s this?

361
00:17:14,820 --> 00:17:16,986
It fits perfectly!

362
00:17:17,009 --> 00:17:18,609
Thank you so much.

363
00:17:18,632 --> 00:17:22,199
We’ll take the scenic route.

364
00:17:22,222 --> 00:17:26,589
Wow, look at that huge bridge!

365
00:17:26,612 --> 00:17:29,745
That’s Rainbow Bridge.

366
00:17:29,768 --> 00:17:32,101
It’s so beautiful!

367
00:17:32,124 --> 00:17:35,017
Can I take a photo?

368
00:17:35,041 --> 00:17:36,508
Sure.

369
00:17:36,530 --> 00:17:39,064
Go ahead and take as many as you like.

370
00:17:39,087 --> 00:17:41,567
Are we almost there?

371
00:17:41,590 --> 00:17:43,044
Of course!

372
00:17:43,068 --> 00:17:45,966
Tokyo Tower is right ahead.

373
00:17:45,989 --> 00:17:49,007
Please stop in front of that entrance.

374
00:17:49,031 --> 00:17:51,198
Certainly.

375
00:17:51,221 --> 00:17:54,088
I’ll pull over in a safe spot.

376
00:17:54,111 --> 00:17:56,364
How much is the fare?

377
00:17:56,387 --> 00:17:59,797
The total comes to 3,200 yen.

378
00:17:59,821 --> 00:18:03,623
Can I pay with a transit IC card?

379
00:18:03,646 --> 00:18:04,887
Of course!

380
00:18:04,911 --> 00:18:06,799
Yes, you can.

381
00:18:06,822 --> 00:18:09,555
Just tap to pay.

382
00:18:09,578 --> 00:18:11,812
Payment complete.

383
00:18:11,836 --> 00:18:14,711
Please watch for any belongings you may have left behind.

384
00:18:14,734 --> 00:18:17,067
Thank you very much.

385
00:18:17,090 --> 00:18:18,590
Scene 8: How to Take Customer Orders

386
00:18:18,590 --> 00:18:20,629
Welcome!

387
00:18:20,652 --> 00:18:24,263
May I take your order?

388
00:18:24,287 --> 00:18:25,932
Hello.

389
00:18:25,956 --> 00:18:28,772
Could I look at the menu first?

390
00:18:28,796 --> 00:18:31,436
Here you are.

391
00:18:31,460 --> 00:18:34,533
Will you be dining in?

392
00:18:34,556 --> 00:18:37,523
Takeout, please.

393
00:18:37,546 --> 00:18:40,154
Takeout, got it.

394
00:18:40,177 --> 00:18:42,577
Certainly.

395
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:45,134
Do you have caffè latte?

396
00:18:45,157 --> 00:18:48,731
Yes, we have both hot and iced.

397
00:18:48,754 --> 00:18:51,754
I’ll have an iced caffè latte, please.

398
00:18:51,777 --> 00:18:55,144
What size would you like?

399
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:58,014
What sizes do you have?

400
00:18:58,037 --> 00:19:02,015
We have Short, Regular, and Large.

401
00:19:02,038 --> 00:19:04,732
Regular, please.

402
00:19:04,756 --> 00:19:07,889
How about sugar or milk?

403
00:19:07,912 --> 00:19:10,845
No sugar, please.

404
00:19:10,868 --> 00:19:14,035
Would you like to adjust the ice?

405
00:19:14,058 --> 00:19:17,025
Could I get less ice?

406
00:19:17,048 --> 00:19:20,917
Sure, I’ll make it with light ice.

407
00:19:20,941 --> 00:19:24,399
Can I substitute regular milk with soy milk?

408
00:19:24,422 --> 00:19:29,488
You can upgrade to a soy latte for just an extra 50 yen.

409
00:19:29,511 --> 00:19:32,445
Then, I'll go with the soy milk, please.

410
00:19:32,468 --> 00:19:35,534
Would you like to add anything else to your order?

411
00:19:35,557 --> 00:19:39,728
I'd like to buy some cake too. What do you have?

412
00:19:39,751 --> 00:19:43,551
We recommend our cheesecake and matcha tart.

413
00:19:43,574 --> 00:19:46,352
I'll take one matcha tart, please.

414
00:19:46,375 --> 00:19:48,509
Certainly.

415
00:19:48,532 --> 00:19:51,898
I'll put it in a takeout box for you.

416
00:19:51,921 --> 00:19:54,155
Could I get a bag as well?

417
00:19:54,178 --> 00:19:57,072
We'll provide a paper bag for you.

418
00:19:57,095 --> 00:19:58,629
Thank you so much.

419
00:19:58,652 --> 00:20:01,685
Would you like to wait inside?

420
00:20:01,708 --> 00:20:04,541
Yes, I'll wait here.

421
00:20:04,564 --> 00:20:07,433
We'll handle the payment first.

422
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,623
How much will that be?

423
00:20:09,646 --> 00:20:13,879
Your drink and cake come to 880 yen.

424
00:20:13,902 --> 00:20:16,269
Can I pay with PayPay?

425
00:20:16,292 --> 00:20:19,766
Yes, please show the barcode.

426
00:20:19,789 --> 00:20:22,356
Okay, it's been scanned.

427
00:20:22,379 --> 00:20:24,946
Thank you so much.

428
00:20:24,969 --> 00:20:27,935
Here's your receipt and calling number.

429
00:20:27,958 --> 00:20:30,440
Will you call out the number?

430
00:20:30,464 --> 00:20:35,162
Yes, we'll call number 5 when your order is ready.

431
00:20:35,186 --> 00:20:37,002
Understood.

432
00:20:37,025 --> 00:20:39,058
I'll sit and wait.

433
00:20:39,081 --> 00:20:42,148
Your order is ready.

434
00:20:42,171 --> 00:20:44,704
Customer number 5.

435
00:20:44,727 --> 00:20:47,361
Yes, that's me.

436
00:20:47,384 --> 00:20:49,384
Thank you so much.

437
00:20:49,408 --> 00:20:50,908
Scene 9: Asking for Help in Japanese

438
00:20:50,908 --> 00:20:52,686
Excuse me.

439
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:54,709
Please help me!

440
00:20:54,732 --> 00:20:57,099
What happened?

441
00:20:57,122 --> 00:20:59,155
Are you okay?

442
00:20:59,178 --> 00:21:02,545
I've lost my wallet.

443
00:21:02,568 --> 00:21:05,401
That's terrible.

444
00:21:05,424 --> 00:21:07,824
Please try to stay calm.

445
00:21:07,847 --> 00:21:10,980
I don't know where I dropped it.

446
00:21:11,003 --> 00:21:14,487
When was the last time you saw your wallet?

447
00:21:14,511 --> 00:21:18,349
About an hour ago, I was at a café.

448
00:21:18,372 --> 00:21:21,444
Do you remember which café?

449
00:21:21,468 --> 00:21:25,001
It was a small red shop near the station.

450
00:21:25,024 --> 00:21:27,630
Was it Starbucks, maybe?

451
00:21:27,654 --> 00:21:33,054
No, I don’t know the name, but it was a small shop.

452
00:21:33,077 --> 00:21:36,910
Can you describe the color and shape of your wallet?

453
00:21:36,933 --> 00:21:40,667
It's a black leather bifold wallet.

454
00:21:40,690 --> 00:21:43,723
What was inside it?

455
00:21:43,746 --> 00:21:47,588
There was cash and a credit card inside.

456
00:21:47,611 --> 00:21:50,648
Was your passport in it too?

457
00:21:50,672 --> 00:21:54,238
No, my passport is at the hotel.

458
00:21:54,261 --> 00:21:56,795
That's a relief.

459
00:21:56,818 --> 00:21:59,818
May I have your name, please?

460
00:21:59,841 --> 00:22:02,107
John Smith.

461
00:22:02,130 --> 00:22:06,197
Do you have a contact phone number?

462
00:22:06,220 --> 00:22:08,953
Is the hotel's phone number okay?

463
00:22:08,976 --> 00:22:10,510
Of course!

464
00:22:10,533 --> 00:22:13,980
Yes, please write down the hotel's name and number.

465
00:22:14,004 --> 00:22:16,137
I've written it down here.

466
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:20,132
Let me prepare the lost property report for you.

467
00:22:20,155 --> 00:22:22,989
I'd like to cancel my credit card.

468
00:22:23,011 --> 00:22:26,678
You should call the card company right away.

469
00:22:26,701 --> 00:22:30,634
Could you help me look up their phone number?

470
00:22:30,657 --> 00:22:31,940
Of course!

471
00:22:31,964 --> 00:22:34,930
Let's look it up on this computer.

472
00:22:34,953 --> 00:22:37,368
Thank you so much!

473
00:22:37,391 --> 00:22:41,688
Here's the number for your card company.

474
00:22:41,712 --> 00:22:44,278
I'll call them right now.

475
00:22:44,301 --> 00:22:47,136
You can use the phone here at the police box.

476
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:48,696
Thank you so much.

477
00:22:48,719 --> 00:22:50,804
That really helps.

478
00:22:50,828 --> 00:22:54,516
I'll call your hotel if your wallet is found.

479
00:22:54,540 --> 00:23:01,038
I hope it turns up... In Japan, lost items are often returned.

480
00:23:01,061 --> 00:23:03,728
That makes me feel better.

481
00:23:03,751 --> 00:23:07,918
Do you know how to get to the hotel you're staying at tonight?

482
00:23:07,941 --> 00:23:11,474
Actually, I've gotten lost too.

483
00:23:11,497 --> 00:23:16,530
I'll print out a map for you.

484
00:23:16,553 --> 00:23:18,593
I really appreciate your kindness.

485
00:23:18,617 --> 00:23:22,150
Please take care on your way back to the hotel.

486
00:23:22,173 --> 00:23:23,673
Scene 10: Hotel Check-Out – A Smooth Departure Guide

487
00:23:23,673 --> 00:23:26,155
Good morning.

488
00:23:26,179 --> 00:23:28,114
Checking out today?

489
00:23:28,137 --> 00:23:32,804
Yes, I'd like to check out, please.

490
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:36,228
May I have your room key, please?

491
00:23:36,251 --> 00:23:40,691
It's room 305.

492
00:23:40,714 --> 00:23:42,354
Here you go.

493
00:23:42,377 --> 00:23:44,377
Thank you so much.

494
00:23:44,400 --> 00:23:48,434
Did you have any drinks from the room?

495
00:23:48,457 --> 00:23:51,823
I had some water from the fridge.

496
00:23:51,846 --> 00:23:55,455
The water is 200 yen per bottle.

497
00:23:55,478 --> 00:23:58,012
I’ll pay in cash.

498
00:23:58,035 --> 00:23:59,635
Here you go.

499
00:23:59,658 --> 00:24:03,141
I'll take exactly 200 yen.

500
00:24:03,164 --> 00:24:05,731
How was your stay with us?

501
00:24:05,754 --> 00:24:08,887
It was very comfortable.

502
00:24:08,910 --> 00:24:11,802
We're so glad to hear that.

503
00:24:11,825 --> 00:24:16,203
The room was clean, and the breakfast was delicious.

504
00:24:16,227 --> 00:24:17,829
Thank you so much.

505
00:24:17,852 --> 00:24:20,985
I'll pass that along to our kitchen staff.

506
00:24:21,008 --> 00:24:24,419
Your check-out is all set.

507
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:29,309
Could you hold my luggage until this evening?

508
00:24:29,332 --> 00:24:33,026
Of course, we'd be happy to.

509
00:24:33,049 --> 00:24:37,216
I have two suitcases.

510
00:24:37,239 --> 00:24:40,474
I'll attach this tag for you.

511
00:24:40,497 --> 00:24:42,330
Is this a claim ticket?

512
00:24:42,353 --> 00:24:43,925
Of course!

513
00:24:43,949 --> 00:24:47,482
Please keep this number tag safe and don't lose it.

514
00:24:47,505 --> 00:24:49,356
Understood.

515
00:24:49,380 --> 00:24:52,231
What time can I pick it up by?

516
00:24:52,254 --> 00:24:55,949
Please come back by 8 PM tonight.

517
00:24:55,973 --> 00:25:00,906
My Shinkansen leaves at 7, so I'll be back by 6.

518
00:25:00,929 --> 00:25:03,015
Understood.

519
00:25:03,039 --> 00:25:05,439
We'll be waiting for you.

520
00:25:05,462 --> 00:25:09,866
Is there a good soba restaurant nearby?

521
00:25:09,889 --> 00:25:14,489
There's a famous soba place right behind the hotel.

522
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:16,350
Is it within walking distance?

523
00:25:16,373 --> 00:25:17,973
Of course!

524
00:25:17,996 --> 00:25:20,396
It's about a 3-minute walk.

525
00:25:20,419 --> 00:25:22,819
I'll check it out.

526
00:25:22,842 --> 00:25:26,376
Would you like a map to the restaurant?

527
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:27,850
Please.

528
00:25:27,874 --> 00:25:31,649
It's the location marked with the red pin on this map.

529
00:25:31,672 --> 00:25:33,872
That's easy to understand.

530
00:25:33,895 --> 00:25:35,495
Thank you so much.

531
00:25:35,518 --> 00:25:39,285
Have a wonderful day today!

532
00:25:39,308 --> 00:25:43,108
The staff here were so kind.

533
00:25:43,131 --> 00:25:47,071
I'm truly honored to hear that.

534
00:25:47,094 --> 00:25:51,294
If I come to Japan again, I'll stay here.

535
00:25:51,317 --> 00:25:54,131
We look forward to your next visit.

536
00:25:54,155 --> 00:25:58,555
I'll come back later to pick up my luggage.

537
00:25:58,578 --> 00:26:00,350
Take care, and see you soon!

538
00:26:00,373 --> 00:26:02,740
We'll be waiting for you.

539
00:26:02,763 --> 00:26:04,263
Scene 11: How to Purchase a Shinkansen Ticket

540
00:26:04,263 --> 00:26:06,396
Welcome!

541
00:26:06,419 --> 00:26:10,266
I'd like to buy a Shinkansen ticket.

542
00:26:10,290 --> 00:26:13,490
Where would you like to go?

543
00:26:13,514 --> 00:26:16,606
I want to go to Kyoto.

544
00:26:16,630 --> 00:26:18,671
Kyoto, got it.

545
00:26:18,694 --> 00:26:21,563
Are you departing today?

546
00:26:21,586 --> 00:26:25,519
Yes, I'd like to take a train this afternoon.

547
00:26:25,542 --> 00:26:27,776
Certainly.

548
00:26:27,799 --> 00:26:32,492
Would you prefer reserved or non-reserved seating?

549
00:26:32,515 --> 00:26:35,292
Reserved seating, please.

550
00:26:35,316 --> 00:26:38,882
What time would you prefer?

551
00:26:38,905 --> 00:26:42,905
Is there a train around 12 PM?

552
00:26:42,928 --> 00:26:47,339
There's a Hikari train departing at 12:05 PM.

553
00:26:47,363 --> 00:26:49,429
I'll take that one.

554
00:26:49,452 --> 00:26:52,819
Do you have a seating preference?

555
00:26:52,842 --> 00:26:56,709
Is there a seat on the side with a view of Mt. Fuji?

556
00:26:56,732 --> 00:26:58,215
Of course!

557
00:26:58,239 --> 00:27:01,681
Seat E is on the Mt. Fuji side.

558
00:27:01,705 --> 00:27:05,387
I'd like a seat with a view of Mt. Fuji, please.

559
00:27:05,410 --> 00:27:07,468
Understood.

560
00:27:07,492 --> 00:27:10,825
I'll reserve a window-side E seat for you.

561
00:27:10,848 --> 00:27:12,615
Thank you so much.

562
00:27:12,638 --> 00:27:16,933
Is it just one adult?

563
00:27:16,956 --> 00:27:19,756
Yes, just me.

564
00:27:19,779 --> 00:27:21,422
One way?

565
00:27:21,446 --> 00:27:23,179
Or round trip?

566
00:27:23,202 --> 00:27:26,085
One way, please.

567
00:27:26,109 --> 00:27:30,767
The total comes to 13,800 yen.

568
00:27:30,791 --> 00:27:33,726
Can I pay with a credit card?

569
00:27:33,749 --> 00:27:37,349
Please insert your payment into this machine.

570
00:27:37,372 --> 00:27:39,840
Okay, I've inserted it.

571
00:27:39,864 --> 00:27:42,864
Please enter your PIN.

572
00:27:42,887 --> 00:27:45,053
I've entered it.

573
00:27:45,076 --> 00:27:46,732
Thank you so much.

574
00:27:46,756 --> 00:27:49,156
Please take your ticket.

575
00:27:49,179 --> 00:27:54,112
Are there any shops or food carts on board?

576
00:27:54,135 --> 00:27:58,771
Yes, they sell bento boxes and drinks from a cart.

577
00:27:58,795 --> 00:28:01,528
I'd like to buy a bento box too.

578
00:28:01,551 --> 00:28:05,518
There are also great bento shops on the platform.

579
00:28:05,541 --> 00:28:07,474
I see.

580
00:28:07,497 --> 00:28:09,988
I'll check them out before boarding.

581
00:28:10,011 --> 00:28:14,066
The Shinkansen departs from Platform 14.

582
00:28:14,090 --> 00:28:16,709
Platform 14, got it.

583
00:28:16,733 --> 00:28:18,866
Understood.

584
00:28:18,889 --> 00:28:22,731
Please wait on the platform at least five minutes before departure.

585
00:28:22,754 --> 00:28:26,788
Thank you for your kind assistance.

586
00:28:26,811 --> 00:28:29,777
Have a fantastic trip!

587
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:31,300
Scene 12: Hot Spring Bath Procedure

588
00:28:31,300 --> 00:28:33,189
Welcome!

589
00:28:33,212 --> 00:28:35,746
A day trip bath?

590
00:28:35,769 --> 00:28:39,302
Yes, I'd like to enjoy an onsen.

591
00:28:39,325 --> 00:28:41,258
Certainly.

592
00:28:41,281 --> 00:28:45,248
That'll be 1,000 yen for one adult.

593
00:28:45,271 --> 00:28:47,804
Here's the bathing fee.

594
00:28:47,827 --> 00:28:50,395
Yes, that's 1,000 yen.

595
00:28:50,419 --> 00:28:52,264
Thank you so much.

596
00:28:52,288 --> 00:28:56,025
Um, are towels included?

597
00:28:56,049 --> 00:28:59,917
No, towels are an additional charge.

598
00:28:59,941 --> 00:29:02,974
Can I rent towels?

599
00:29:02,997 --> 00:29:09,764
Yes, a face towel is 200 yen, and a bath towel is 300 yen.

600
00:29:09,787 --> 00:29:11,991
I'd like both, please.

601
00:29:12,014 --> 00:29:14,347
Certainly.

602
00:29:14,370 --> 00:29:16,983
That'll be 500 yen for the set.

603
00:29:17,007 --> 00:29:19,245
Here you are.

604
00:29:19,268 --> 00:29:21,038
Thank you so much.

605
00:29:21,061 --> 00:29:24,028
I'll hand you the towels now.

606
00:29:24,051 --> 00:29:27,728
Are there any rules for using the onsen?

607
00:29:27,752 --> 00:29:31,011
There are a few important etiquette rules.

608
00:29:31,034 --> 00:29:32,925
Please tell me.

609
00:29:32,949 --> 00:29:38,015
First, wash your body before entering the bath.

610
00:29:38,038 --> 00:29:41,306
I'll wash up before getting in.

611
00:29:41,330 --> 00:29:42,944
Of course!

612
00:29:42,968 --> 00:29:47,101
Please clean yourself thoroughly at the washing area.

613
00:29:47,124 --> 00:29:48,491
Understood.

614
00:29:48,514 --> 00:29:52,047
Can I put my towel in the bath?

615
00:29:52,070 --> 00:29:56,157
No, you must not put towels in the bath.

616
00:29:56,181 --> 00:29:58,981
What should I do with my towel?

617
00:29:59,004 --> 00:30:03,804
Place it on your head or on the edge of the bath.

618
00:30:03,827 --> 00:30:05,502
Understood.

619
00:30:05,525 --> 00:30:08,558
What about people with long hair?

620
00:30:08,581 --> 00:30:13,115
Please tie it up so it doesn’t touch the water.

621
00:30:13,139 --> 00:30:14,939
Got it.

622
00:30:14,962 --> 00:30:18,695
Are there lockers in the changing room?

623
00:30:18,718 --> 00:30:19,966
Of course!

624
00:30:19,989 --> 00:30:22,637
Yes, we have lockers with keys.

625
00:30:22,661 --> 00:30:25,309
I can store my valuables there, right?

626
00:30:25,333 --> 00:30:26,820
Of course!

627
00:30:26,843 --> 00:30:30,443
Please wear the key on your wrist while bathing.

628
00:30:30,466 --> 00:30:34,033
Can I buy drinks after my bath?

629
00:30:34,056 --> 00:30:39,189
There are vending machines for milk and juice in the lounge area.

630
00:30:39,212 --> 00:30:41,179
I'm looking forward to it!

631
00:30:41,201 --> 00:30:42,935
Off I go!

632
00:30:42,958 --> 00:30:45,891
Please relax and enjoy your time.

633
00:30:45,914 --> 00:30:47,414
Scene 13: Shinkansen Reservation Changes and Luggage Size Requirements

634
00:30:47,414 --> 00:30:51,783
How may I assist you today?

635
00:30:51,806 --> 00:30:55,940
I'd like to change my Shinkansen reservation for tomorrow.

636
00:30:55,963 --> 00:30:57,736
I see, you'd like to make a change.

637
00:30:57,759 --> 00:31:01,646
May I see your ticket, please?

638
00:31:01,670 --> 00:31:04,403
Yes, here it is.

639
00:31:04,426 --> 00:31:06,305
Thank you so much.

640
00:31:06,329 --> 00:31:09,227
How would you like to change it?

641
00:31:09,250 --> 00:31:12,284
I have a large suitcase.

642
00:31:12,307 --> 00:31:14,840
That *is* a large piece of luggage.

643
00:31:14,863 --> 00:31:18,138
What are the dimensions of your luggage?

644
00:31:18,162 --> 00:31:23,979
The total of the length, width, and height is 180 centimeters.

645
00:31:24,002 --> 00:31:29,572
In that case, you'll need to reserve an oversized luggage space.

646
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:32,444
Can't I just place it at a regular seat?

647
00:31:32,468 --> 00:31:33,923
Of course!

648
00:31:33,946 --> 00:31:40,680
Luggage exceeding a total of 160 centimeters requires a reservation.

649
00:31:40,703 --> 00:31:43,669
Is there a place to put my luggage?

650
00:31:43,692 --> 00:31:48,695
There's space behind the last row of seats in the car.

651
00:31:48,719 --> 00:31:53,486
Can I change to a seat with that space?

652
00:31:53,509 --> 00:31:57,283
Please let us know your preferred time for tomorrow.

653
00:31:57,306 --> 00:32:01,284
The train around 10 AM would be perfect.

654
00:32:01,307 --> 00:32:03,953
I’ll check for available seats.

655
00:32:03,976 --> 00:32:06,010
Just a moment, please.

656
00:32:06,033 --> 00:32:07,966
Thank you.

657
00:32:07,989 --> 00:32:13,801
There’s an available oversized baggage area on the 10:15 AM train.

658
00:32:13,824 --> 00:32:15,958
That’s great!

659
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:18,314
I’ll take that seat.

660
00:32:18,337 --> 00:32:22,546
Your seat will be by the window in the last row.

661
00:32:22,569 --> 00:32:27,003
Can I place my luggage right behind my seat?

662
00:32:27,026 --> 00:32:28,628
Of course!

663
00:32:28,651 --> 00:32:32,269
That’s a designated space for passengers with reservations.

664
00:32:32,292 --> 00:32:35,629
Is there an extra fee?

665
00:32:35,653 --> 00:32:40,460
No additional charge if you book in advance.

666
00:32:40,483 --> 00:32:43,052
So, I can change it for free?

667
00:32:43,076 --> 00:32:44,609
Of course!

668
00:32:44,632 --> 00:32:47,799
Here’s your new ticket.

669
00:32:47,822 --> 00:32:49,658
Let me check.

670
00:32:49,681 --> 00:32:53,814
It says 'with oversized baggage space.'

671
00:32:53,837 --> 00:32:55,251
Of course!

672
00:32:55,275 --> 00:32:57,242
That’s correct.

673
00:32:57,265 --> 00:33:00,363
Thank you so much for your help!

674
00:33:00,386 --> 00:33:03,469
Have a safe trip!

675
00:33:03,493 --> 00:33:04,993
Scene 14: How to Refuel Gasoline

676
00:33:04,993 --> 00:33:08,160
Welcome!

677
00:33:08,183 --> 00:33:11,249
You need to refuel, right?

678
00:33:11,272 --> 00:33:13,713
Yes, please.

679
00:33:13,737 --> 00:33:17,357
Which type of fuel would you like?

680
00:33:17,380 --> 00:33:22,581
It’s a rental car—what should I use?

681
00:33:22,604 --> 00:33:29,537
Please check the inside of the fuel flap or the vehicle registration certificate.

682
00:33:29,560 --> 00:33:33,327
There’s a red sticker.

683
00:33:33,350 --> 00:33:37,489
A red sticker means regular gasoline.

684
00:33:37,512 --> 00:33:40,946
Fill it up with regular, please.

685
00:33:40,969 --> 00:33:43,202
Certainly.

686
00:33:43,225 --> 00:33:47,992
May I clean your windows?

687
00:33:48,015 --> 00:33:50,499
Yes, please.

688
00:33:50,522 --> 00:33:53,889
Do you have any ashtray waste or trash?

689
00:33:53,912 --> 00:33:56,912
No trash here.

690
00:33:56,935 --> 00:33:59,468
Certainly.

691
00:33:59,491 --> 00:34:03,987
Please wait a moment while we finish refueling.

692
00:34:04,010 --> 00:34:08,610
You’ll need to show the receipt to the rental car company.

693
00:34:08,633 --> 00:34:11,400
The receipt, right?

694
00:34:11,423 --> 00:34:16,837
We’ll issue it along with a full-tank certificate.

695
00:34:16,860 --> 00:34:19,193
That really helps.

696
00:34:19,216 --> 00:34:21,850
Thank you for waiting.

697
00:34:21,873 --> 00:34:27,073
Refueling is complete.

698
00:34:27,096 --> 00:34:29,387
How much is it?

699
00:34:29,411 --> 00:34:34,217
The total comes to 4,500 yen.

700
00:34:34,240 --> 00:34:37,458
Can I pay with a credit card?

701
00:34:37,482 --> 00:34:41,015
Yes, this card is accepted.

702
00:34:41,038 --> 00:34:45,171
I’ll pay with this card.

703
00:34:45,194 --> 00:34:49,794
Please provide your signature or PIN.

704
00:34:49,817 --> 00:34:54,220
Okay, I’ve entered my PIN.

705
00:34:54,244 --> 00:34:56,222
Thank you so much.

706
00:34:56,245 --> 00:35:01,016
Here’s your card and receipt with the full-tank certificate.

707
00:35:01,039 --> 00:35:06,496
It says 'full tank,' right?

708
00:35:06,520 --> 00:35:10,218
Yes, please show this to the rental car company.

709
00:35:10,241 --> 00:35:14,500
Is the rental car return location nearby?

710
00:35:14,524 --> 00:35:19,260
Yes, just turn right at this intersection—it’s right there.

711
00:35:19,283 --> 00:35:21,117
Understood.

712
00:35:21,140 --> 00:35:23,740
It’s that close?

713
00:35:23,763 --> 00:35:31,840
The staff will check for any damage when you return it.

714
00:35:31,864 --> 00:35:35,945
Got it! I’ll drive safely.

715
00:35:35,968 --> 00:35:37,901
Thank you very much.

716
00:35:37,924 --> 00:35:40,324
Take care!

717
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:41,847
Scene 15: Kimono Rental Process

718
00:35:41,847 --> 00:35:44,096
Welcome!

719
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:47,253
Welcome to our Kimono Rental!

720
00:35:47,276 --> 00:35:48,810
Hello.

721
00:35:48,833 --> 00:35:51,689
I'd like to rent a kimono.

722
00:35:51,712 --> 00:35:54,571
Do you have a reservation?

723
00:35:54,594 --> 00:35:58,128
Yes, I booked online.

724
00:35:58,151 --> 00:36:01,970
May I have your name, please?

725
00:36:01,993 --> 00:36:03,827
Smith.

726
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:06,301
Mr. Smith, correct?

727
00:36:06,324 --> 00:36:10,890
Today, you've chosen our kimono dressing and hair styling plan.

728
00:36:10,913 --> 00:36:13,748
Yes, that's the one.

729
00:36:13,772 --> 00:36:18,573
First, please choose your favorite kimono from these.

730
00:36:18,596 --> 00:36:22,963
There are so many—I can't decide!

731
00:36:22,986 --> 00:36:27,070
Pink and red are very popular choices.

732
00:36:27,093 --> 00:36:30,860
This blue kimono is beautiful.

733
00:36:30,883 --> 00:36:33,684
I’ll go with this color.

734
00:36:33,707 --> 00:36:36,676
That’s a lovely choice!

735
00:36:36,700 --> 00:36:39,997
Next, let’s pick an obi sash.

736
00:36:40,020 --> 00:36:43,229
Which obi would you like?

737
00:36:43,253 --> 00:36:48,187
A yellow or white obi would look adorable with it.

738
00:36:48,210 --> 00:36:52,305
I’ll go with the yellow one, then.

739
00:36:52,328 --> 00:36:56,022
What size tabi socks do you need for your footwear?

740
00:36:56,046 --> 00:37:00,865
My foot size is 24 centimeters.

741
00:37:00,889 --> 00:37:05,295
I’ll prepare tabi socks in size 24 for you.

742
00:37:05,318 --> 00:37:09,085
How long does the dressing take?

743
00:37:09,108 --> 00:37:14,241
The dressing and hair styling will take about 30 minutes.

744
00:37:14,264 --> 00:37:16,998
Please go ahead with the dressing.

745
00:37:17,021 --> 00:37:21,296
Please head to the changing room on the second floor.

746
00:37:21,319 --> 00:37:25,289
Can I leave my bag and clothes here?

747
00:37:25,312 --> 00:37:29,999
Yes, we can store your large belongings for you.

748
00:37:30,022 --> 00:37:31,598
Thank you so much.

749
00:37:31,622 --> 00:37:33,822
Does it feel too tight?

750
00:37:33,845 --> 00:37:36,579
It fits perfectly!

751
00:37:36,602 --> 00:37:38,802
Thank you for waiting.

752
00:37:38,825 --> 00:37:41,760
It looks wonderful on you!

753
00:37:41,783 --> 00:37:45,158
Wow, I’m so happy!

754
00:37:45,182 --> 00:37:49,582
Please return to the shop by 5 PM.

755
00:37:49,605 --> 00:37:51,855
By 5 PM, got it.

756
00:37:51,878 --> 00:37:53,934
Understood.

757
00:37:53,958 --> 00:37:58,011
Enjoy exploring the city!

758
00:37:58,034 --> 00:37:59,680
Off I go!

759
00:37:59,703 --> 00:38:01,203
Scene 16: Buying Tickets at an Art Museum

760
00:38:01,203 --> 00:38:03,237
Welcome!

761
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:05,677
Ticket counter.

762
00:38:05,700 --> 00:38:09,067
Two adult tickets, please.

763
00:38:09,089 --> 00:38:11,760
Same-day tickets, correct?

764
00:38:11,784 --> 00:38:15,479
Yes, can we enter now?

765
00:38:15,503 --> 00:38:19,315
Yes, you may enter right away.

766
00:38:19,338 --> 00:38:22,180
How much is a same-day ticket?

767
00:38:22,203 --> 00:38:27,770
It’s 2,000 yen per person, so 4,000 yen in total.

768
00:38:27,793 --> 00:38:31,193
Here’s 4,000 yen.

769
00:38:31,216 --> 00:38:32,849
Thank you so much.

770
00:38:32,872 --> 00:38:35,939
Here are your tickets and a pamphlet.

771
00:38:35,962 --> 00:38:40,128
Is it okay to take photos inside?

772
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:45,318
Photography is generally allowed, but no flash.

773
00:38:45,341 --> 00:38:48,546
So, no flash—got it.

774
00:38:48,569 --> 00:38:52,736
Yes, and please refrain from recording videos.

775
00:38:52,759 --> 00:38:54,638
Understood.

776
00:38:54,661 --> 00:38:56,956
I’ll just take photos.

777
00:38:56,980 --> 00:39:01,613
Also, please store large backpacks in the lockers.

778
00:39:01,636 --> 00:39:05,203
Where are the coin lockers?

779
00:39:05,226 --> 00:39:08,792
They’re to the left after you enter.

780
00:39:08,815 --> 00:39:12,149
Do I get the 100-yen coin back?

781
00:39:12,172 --> 00:39:16,857
Yes, it's the type where you get 100 yen back after use.

782
00:39:16,880 --> 00:39:18,213
That’s great!

783
00:39:18,236 --> 00:39:22,770
Can I leave and re-enter later?

784
00:39:22,793 --> 00:39:26,999
You can re-enter if you get a stamp at the exit.

785
00:39:27,022 --> 00:39:30,956
That’s great—I’d like to grab lunch outside.

786
00:39:30,979 --> 00:39:35,012
Please let the staff know when you’re leaving.

787
00:39:35,035 --> 00:39:36,890
Understood.

788
00:39:36,914 --> 00:39:40,480
How long does it take to tour the exhibit?

789
00:39:40,503 --> 00:39:45,437
It takes about an hour and a half to see everything.

790
00:39:45,461 --> 00:39:48,061
I’ll take my time exploring.

791
00:39:48,084 --> 00:39:53,684
There’s also a special exhibit in the back—don’t miss it!

792
00:39:53,707 --> 00:39:55,961
I’ll check that out too.

793
00:39:55,985 --> 00:39:57,485
Scene 17: Consultation for Headache Medication

794
00:39:57,485 --> 00:40:02,085
Hello, how can I help you today?

795
00:40:02,108 --> 00:40:03,845
I have a headache.

796
00:40:03,868 --> 00:40:06,719
When did the pain start?

797
00:40:06,743 --> 00:40:10,143
It’s been hurting since this morning.

798
00:40:10,165 --> 00:40:12,899
Do you have a fever?

799
00:40:12,923 --> 00:40:15,566
No, I don’t.

800
00:40:15,590 --> 00:40:18,644
Are you taking any cold medicine?

801
00:40:18,668 --> 00:40:22,474
Are you looking for something to relieve the pain?

802
00:40:22,498 --> 00:40:26,098
Yes, I’d like some headache medication.

803
00:40:26,121 --> 00:40:29,887
Are you currently taking any other medications?

804
00:40:29,910 --> 00:40:33,444
No, nothing in particular.

805
00:40:33,467 --> 00:40:36,473
Do you have any allergies to medication?

806
00:40:36,496 --> 00:40:39,463
No, I don’t.

807
00:40:39,486 --> 00:40:43,739
I recommend this fever and pain reliever.

808
00:40:43,763 --> 00:40:46,496
How should I take it?

809
00:40:46,519 --> 00:40:50,886
Take it three times a day after meals.

810
00:40:50,909 --> 00:40:54,042
Do I *have* to take it after meals?

811
00:40:54,065 --> 00:40:59,532
To avoid stomach irritation, try to eat something before taking it.

812
00:40:59,555 --> 00:41:01,555
Understood.

813
00:41:01,577 --> 00:41:04,145
How many pills should I take at once?

814
00:41:04,168 --> 00:41:08,002
Take two tablets at a time.

815
00:41:08,026 --> 00:41:11,882
How long should I wait between doses?

816
00:41:11,906 --> 00:41:15,639
Please wait at least four hours between doses.

817
00:41:15,662 --> 00:41:19,513
Do you have any medicine for stomachaches too?

818
00:41:19,537 --> 00:41:23,513
Would you like to get some stomach medicine as well?

819
00:41:23,536 --> 00:41:27,550
Yes, I ate too much and my stomach hurts.

820
00:41:27,574 --> 00:41:32,614
Then I’ll give you this stomach medicine too.

821
00:41:32,637 --> 00:41:35,448
Does this contain any drowsiness-inducing ingredients?

822
00:41:35,471 --> 00:41:40,117
This headache medicine may cause slight drowsiness.

823
00:41:40,141 --> 00:41:44,786
That’s fine—I’m not driving today.

824
00:41:44,809 --> 00:41:47,102
Good to hear.

825
00:41:47,125 --> 00:41:49,792
Take care and feel better soon!

826
00:41:49,815 --> 00:41:52,148
Thank you so much.

827
00:41:52,171 --> 00:41:53,671
Scene 18: Ordering Takoyaki at a Street Stall

828
00:41:53,671 --> 00:41:56,162
Welcome!

829
00:41:56,186 --> 00:41:58,719
That smells amazing!

830
00:41:58,742 --> 00:42:01,109
What kind of stall is this?

831
00:42:01,132 --> 00:42:05,498
It’s a takoyaki and okonomiyaki stand!

832
00:42:05,521 --> 00:42:08,210
I’ll take one order of takoyaki, please.

833
00:42:08,234 --> 00:42:12,634
Sure thing—one box of takoyaki coming up!

834
00:42:12,657 --> 00:42:15,700
Can I choose the seasoning?

835
00:42:15,724 --> 00:42:20,257
We’ve got sauce, soy sauce, and ponzu!

836
00:42:20,280 --> 00:42:23,247
Which one is the most popular?

837
00:42:23,270 --> 00:42:28,003
The classic sauce flavor is always the favorite.

838
00:42:28,026 --> 00:42:31,307
Then I'll go with the sauce flavor, please.

839
00:42:31,331 --> 00:42:35,380
You can add mayonnaise and dried seaweed flakes if you'd like.

840
00:42:35,404 --> 00:42:39,137
Yes, please put lots on!

841
00:42:39,160 --> 00:42:43,167
I'll pile on so much bonito flakes they'll be dancing.

842
00:42:43,191 --> 00:42:44,767
Thank you so much.

843
00:42:44,791 --> 00:42:47,400
Can I eat it here?

844
00:42:47,423 --> 00:42:52,757
There are benches by the food stall, so you can eat there.

845
00:42:52,780 --> 00:42:55,852
It looks freshly grilled and piping hot!

846
00:42:55,875 --> 00:43:00,809
The inside is really hot, so be careful not to burn yourself.

847
00:43:00,832 --> 00:43:04,681
Okay, I'll be careful while eating.

848
00:43:04,704 --> 00:43:07,937
Your total comes to 600 yen.

849
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:11,233
Can I use a credit card?

850
00:43:11,257 --> 00:43:16,149
Sorry, we only accept cash.

851
00:43:16,172 --> 00:43:18,179
Understood.

852
00:43:18,203 --> 00:43:20,823
I’ll pay in cash.

853
00:43:20,846 --> 00:43:23,916
I'll take the exact amount.

854
00:43:23,939 --> 00:43:27,106
Do you sell drinks as well?

855
00:43:27,129 --> 00:43:31,295
We have cold ramune and canned beer.

856
00:43:31,318 --> 00:43:34,594
I'll add a ramune, please.

857
00:43:34,618 --> 00:43:40,251
Sure thing! That'll be an additional 200 yen, making it 800 yen in total.

858
00:43:40,274 --> 00:43:43,571
I don't know how to open this bottle.

859
00:43:43,595 --> 00:43:47,361
Press hard on the marble at the top, and it'll open.

860
00:43:47,384 --> 00:43:50,041
Want me to open it for you?

861
00:43:50,065 --> 00:43:51,798
Please.

862
00:43:51,821 --> 00:43:55,040
There you go, it's open!

863
00:43:55,064 --> 00:43:57,744
Enjoy your meal!

864
00:43:57,767 --> 00:44:00,252
Thank you for your kindness.

865
00:44:00,276 --> 00:44:01,776
Scene 19: How to Send International Mail

866
00:44:01,776 --> 00:44:03,976
Welcome!

867
00:44:03,999 --> 00:44:06,855
Please proceed to the postal counter.

868
00:44:06,878 --> 00:44:10,919
I'd like to send this abroad.

869
00:44:10,943 --> 00:44:14,343
Certainly, international mail it is.

870
00:44:14,366 --> 00:44:17,701
Which country are you sending it to?

871
00:44:17,724 --> 00:44:21,058
I'd like to send it to the United States.

872
00:44:21,081 --> 00:44:24,056
What's inside the package?

873
00:44:24,079 --> 00:44:28,133
It contains souvenirs like snacks and some clothes.

874
00:44:28,157 --> 00:44:32,095
Are there any hazardous materials or liquids inside?

875
00:44:32,118 --> 00:44:34,518
No, there aren't.

876
00:44:34,541 --> 00:44:37,874
Let me weigh your package.

877
00:44:37,897 --> 00:44:41,179
Please place it on the scale.

878
00:44:41,203 --> 00:44:44,136
Okay, I've put it on.

879
00:44:44,159 --> 00:44:46,733
It's exactly 2 kilograms.

880
00:44:46,757 --> 00:44:48,991
When will it arrive?

881
00:44:49,014 --> 00:44:54,414
With EMS, it'll arrive in about 5 days by air.

882
00:44:54,436 --> 00:44:58,203
How long does sea mail take?

883
00:44:58,226 --> 00:45:02,626
Sea mail takes about 2 months.

884
00:45:02,649 --> 00:45:07,082
I'd like it to arrive quickly, so I'll go with EMS.

885
00:45:07,105 --> 00:45:09,239
Certainly.

886
00:45:09,262 --> 00:45:12,748
Did you create the label online?

887
00:45:12,772 --> 00:45:17,372
No, I haven't done that yet.

888
00:45:17,395 --> 00:45:22,528
Please enter the address on your smartphone to create the label.

889
00:45:22,551 --> 00:45:25,618
Do you have a guide for how to write it?

890
00:45:25,641 --> 00:45:30,255
Scan this QR code to input the details.

891
00:45:30,278 --> 00:45:32,611
I've finished.

892
00:45:32,634 --> 00:45:34,903
The barcode is ready.

893
00:45:34,927 --> 00:45:36,606
Thank you so much.

894
00:45:36,629 --> 00:45:39,696
I'll print it here for you.

895
00:45:39,719 --> 00:45:45,052
Can I also send my suitcase to a Japanese airport?

896
00:45:45,075 --> 00:45:50,842
Yes, you can use our airport delivery service as well.

897
00:45:50,865 --> 00:45:54,515
How many days before my arrival should I send it?

898
00:45:54,539 --> 00:45:59,539
Please bring it here at least two days before your flight.

899
00:45:59,562 --> 00:46:03,242
It's so convenient to travel hands-free!

900
00:46:03,265 --> 00:46:06,946
We hope you'll use our service again next time.

901
00:46:06,969 --> 00:46:09,784
How much is the shipping fee today?

902
00:46:09,808 --> 00:46:14,183
It'll be 4,500 yen with EMS.

903
00:46:14,207 --> 00:46:17,419
I'll pay with e-money.

904
00:46:17,442 --> 00:46:19,409
Just tap it here.

905
00:46:19,432 --> 00:46:22,116
Thank you very much.

906
00:46:22,139 --> 00:46:23,639
Scene 20: Matcha Experience Lesson

907
00:46:23,639 --> 00:46:25,472
Hello.

908
00:46:25,495 --> 00:46:28,978
Welcome to our matcha experience.

909
00:46:29,002 --> 00:46:30,935
Hello.

910
00:46:30,958 --> 00:46:34,430
I've been looking forward to this all day!

911
00:46:34,454 --> 00:46:36,743
Thank you.

912
00:46:36,766 --> 00:46:40,903
Please enjoy this sweet first.

913
00:46:40,927 --> 00:46:44,127
Do we eat it before drinking the tea?

914
00:46:44,150 --> 00:46:45,810
Of course!

915
00:46:45,833 --> 00:46:51,452
Having something sweet first makes the tea taste even better.

916
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:53,208
I see!

917
00:46:53,231 --> 00:46:55,564
Here I go!

918
00:46:55,587 --> 00:47:00,058
Now, let's try whisking the tea.

919
00:47:00,082 --> 00:47:02,582
How do we drink it?

920
00:47:02,605 --> 00:47:06,742
First, we'll add hot water to the bowl.

921
00:47:06,766 --> 00:47:10,847
We use a bamboo whisk called a *chasen*, right?

922
00:47:10,871 --> 00:47:12,507
Of course!

923
00:47:12,530 --> 00:47:16,930
Use your wrist to move it quickly.

924
00:47:16,953 --> 00:47:19,153
Like this?

925
00:47:19,176 --> 00:47:22,510
The foam isn't forming very well.

926
00:47:22,533 --> 00:47:25,866
Try again.

927
00:47:25,889 --> 00:47:30,730
The trick is to shake your wrist, not your elbow.

928
00:47:30,754 --> 00:47:35,230
Oh, it's foaming nicely now!

929
00:47:35,254 --> 00:47:38,087
You're doing great!

930
00:47:38,110 --> 00:47:41,154
Do we have to sit formally?

931
00:47:41,178 --> 00:47:46,711
If your legs hurt, you can sit more comfortably.

932
00:47:46,734 --> 00:47:49,018
That really helps.

933
00:47:49,041 --> 00:47:52,041
My legs have gone numb!

934
00:47:52,064 --> 00:47:55,998
You can also use a chair if you'd like.

935
00:47:56,021 --> 00:47:59,954
Do we turn the bowl when drinking?

936
00:47:59,977 --> 00:48:01,853
Of course!

937
00:48:01,877 --> 00:48:07,810
Turn it clockwise twice to avoid the front.

938
00:48:07,833 --> 00:48:11,833
It's a gesture of consideration for the other person, isn't it?

939
00:48:11,856 --> 00:48:14,256
Exactly.

940
00:48:14,279 --> 00:48:16,612
You know so much about this!

941
00:48:16,635 --> 00:48:21,693
It's a little bitter, but really delicious.

942
00:48:21,716 --> 00:48:27,250
Finally, slurp it all up to signal you're done.

943
00:48:27,273 --> 00:48:30,750
That's the sign you've finished drinking, right?

944
00:48:30,773 --> 00:48:32,387
Of course!

945
00:48:32,411 --> 00:48:35,944
You did a wonderful job preparing the tea.

946
00:48:35,967 --> 00:48:40,940
I'm so moved to have experienced such a traditional Japanese culture.

947
00:48:40,964 --> 00:48:44,402
I'm glad you enjoyed it!